        <Description>Unlist NuGet package versions programmatically with ease.</Description>
        <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
        <PackageReleaseNotes>See the README and CHANGELOG.md.

## Changes since 0.2.0

### Added
- The `nuversions show` subcommand: a pure read that prints every version of a package — stable
  and pre-release, listed and unlisted — with one `Status=listed|unlisted` line per version.
  It sends no delete request and needs no API key. With `--output json`, same one-object-per-line
  NDJSON schema as `unlist`; a missing package exits `2`.

### Changed
- The project is renamed: the project name `PreReleaseDelist` becomes `NuVersions`, the NuGet id
  `PreReleaseDelist` becomes `NuVersions`, and the `prerelease-delist` command becomes
  `nuversions`. The single command is now a hierarchy: `nuversions unlist` (today's delist
  behavior) and `nuversions show`. The old package id will be deprecated on NuGet.org pointing
  at the new one.
- The unlist status vocabulary now matches nuget.org terminology: `unlisted` / `already-unlisted`
  (was `delisted` / `already-delisted`), with the same exit-code contract.
- The environment-variable fallback prefix is now `NUVERSIONS_`; the generic `NUGET_*` names stay.
- The domain vocabulary is unlist end to end: Delist becomes Unlist, Delisting becomes Unlisting,
  Delisted becomes Unlisted, and Delete becomes Unlist at the contract level. The all-pre-release
  option is now `--unlist-all` (was `--delist-all`). Terms are defined by the Unlist action entry
  in GLOSSARY.md.

### Removed
- The `prerelease-delist` command name and the `PreReleaseDelist` package id.</PackageReleaseNotes>
